# REGRESSION (Rust lane) — `Box[N](p1.node)` reads an enum value out of a
# STILL-LIVE struct field. The source is live, so CoW's rule is
# clone-not-move; the copy used to be SHALLOW, so the copy and `p1` ended up
# owning the SAME inner `Box[N]` children and both dropped them at scope exit:
#
#     free(): double free detected in tcache 2
#
# Under ASan the report is a heap-use-after-free inside the drop chain, with the
# free and the use both reached from `main`'s `W__drop`:
#
#     ERROR: AddressSanitizer: heap-use-after-free
#       #0 N__drop            #1 Box__N__drop
#       #2 N__drop            #3 W__drop            #4 main
#     freed by thread T0 here:
#       #1 __gorget_global_dealloc_fn   #2 __gorget_box_free_N   #3 Box__N__drop
#
# `gg check` ACCEPTED it, so it was a one-sided accept of a memory-unsafe
# program — Core #8: "both backends agree" is not a pass when the agreed-on
# behaviour is a double free.
#
# ⛔ THIS FIXTURE'S ORIGINAL HEADER NAMED THE WRONG DISCRIMINATOR, and the
# correction is the more useful half of the story. It claimed the axis was
# "specifically the nested-`Box` payload whose clone does not recurse", and
# cited a `Leaf(String)` cell as a clean control. Measured: `N__clone` is
# CORRECT and is NEVER CALLED, and the real axis is HEAP vs LITERAL payload —
# `Box[String](w1.s)` with a runtime-built `String` and no `Box` in the payload
# at all double-freed identically. The `Leaf(String)` control was green only
# because string literals are immortal `.rodata` views with `cap = 0`, on which
# `gorget_string_free` no-ops. A control that cannot allocate acquits nothing
# (Core #12). The minimal shape now lives beside this one as
# `known_gaps/box_ctor_field_source_owning_string.gg`.
#
# NOT a use-after-move on the user's part and NOT dependent on aliasing between
# the two sources: the crashing shape reproduced with every leaf distinct and no
# value read twice (l1,l2 -> p1; l3,l4 -> p2; p1,p2 -> p3). It also reproduced
# with a traversal instead of a plain drop.
#
# ⛔ WHY THIS LIVES IN `known_gaps/` DESPITE BEING A PASSING REGRESSION FIXTURE
# WITH A LIVE TEST (the `box_ctor_closure_matches_box_new` precedent): the
# SELF-HOST lane cannot compile the emitted C for a resource field read feeding
# a box mint — it types the read as `void*` and hands that to
# `__gorget_box_alloc_N`. Pre-existing, unrelated to the Rust-lane fix, filed.
# A top-level fixture is auto-scanned into `runtime_parity_corpus`, so it must
# stay out of that directory until the self-host lane can build it.
#
# EXPECTED OUTPUT: built
# EXPECTED EXIT: 0, and clean under ASan.

enum N:
    Leaf(String)
    Pair(Box[N], Box[N])

struct W:
    N node

int main():
    W l1 = W(N.Leaf("aaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaa"))
    W l2 = W(N.Leaf("bbbbbbbbbbbbbbbbbbbbbbbbbbbb"))
    W l3 = W(N.Leaf("cccccccccccccccccccccccccccc"))
    W l4 = W(N.Leaf("dddddddddddddddddddddddddddd"))
    W p1 = W(N.Pair(Box[N](l1.node), Box[N](l2.node)))
    W p2 = W(N.Pair(Box[N](l3.node), Box[N](l4.node)))
    # `p1.node` / `p2.node` are enum values that THEMSELVES own `Box`es, and
    # both structs are still live. The clone taken here must recurse into those
    # inner boxes; before the mint routed through the ownership chokepoint it
    # did not, so they were owned twice and freed twice.
    W p3 = W(N.Pair(Box[N](p1.node), Box[N](p2.node)))
    print("built")
    return 0
